{
  "requirement": "Per-file annotation details in the coverage overview are collapsed\ninitially.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.test-coverage.index.gaps.details.initial` has one obligation. The per-file annotation details in the coverage overview must be collapsed in the initial rendering.\n\n`src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[documented_items_are_counted_once_with_browsable_directory_and_file_groups]` tests this directly. It builds an overview with three documented files: `code.rs` at the root, `src/direct.rs` and `src/deep/nested.rs`. For each one it takes the card from the `file_card` helper. The helper returns the file's button row and its detail row. For every card the test asserts `aria-expanded=\"false\"` on the toggle and ` hidden>` on the detail markup. It also checks that the card still holds the explanation text, the locations and the note links. That shows the details are present but collapsed, and not simply left out.\n\nThe same test asserts that the root file's row is not hidden. It also asserts that no `<details` element and no ` hidden` attribute comes before that row. This rules out a wrong fix that collapses the whole file map or the row itself.\n\nThe directory groups are rendered `open`. That is not per-file annotation detail, so it does not conflict with the requirement.\n\n`src/execution_coverage/check.rs#mod[tests]/fn[book_browses_all_proposals_while_cli_checks_reviews_and_measurements]` runs `exercise_file_click` on the rendered \"Documented coverage gaps\" page. It also checks that the page content survives different review and measurement states. This is only supporting evidence. `exercise_file_click` starts its simulated rows with `hidden: true` and does not read that state from the HTML. The `book.rs` test carries the initial-collapse assertions.\n\nBoth tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no unmarked relevant test and no unaddressed boundary or failure case.",
  "references": "a2cc060e1df2ba2c17447fffb36163d9fcb735a547cf82181693e801777d8489",
